PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/:id/unverify/freelancer
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Replace :id with actual user UUID

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "User unverified as freelancer successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "user-uuid",
###     "name": "John Doe",
###     "isVerifiedAsFreelancer": false,
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### UNVERIFY USER AS CLIENT
### ============================================
### Unverify a user as a client (employee only)
### Sets isVerifiedAsClient to false

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/:id/unverify/client
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Replace :id with actual user UUID

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "User unverified as client successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "user-uuid",
###     "name": "John Doe",
###     "isVerifiedAsClient": false,
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### SUSPEND USER
### ============================================
### Suspend a user account (employee only)
### Sets isSuspended to true and stores the suspension reason

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/:id/suspend
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

{
  "suspendedReason": "Violation of terms and conditions. User engaged in fraudulent activities."
}

### Replace :id with actual user UUID

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "User suspended successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "user-uuid",
###     "name": "John Doe",
###     "isSuspended": true,
###     "suspendedReason": "Violation of terms and conditions. User engaged in fraudulent activities.",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Error Response (Missing Reason):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "suspendedReason",
###       "message": "Suspended reason is required"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### UNSUSPEND USER
### ============================================
### Unsuspend a user account (employee only)
### Sets isSuspended to false and clears the suspension reason

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/:id/unsuspend
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Replace :id with actual user UUID
### No request body required

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "User unsuspended successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "user-uuid",
###     "name": "John Doe",
###     "isSuspended": false,
###     "suspendedReason": null,
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Public endpoints (no auth required):
###      * GET /api/users (get all users)
###      * GET /api/users/:id (get user by ID)
###    - User endpoints (requires user JWT token):
###      * GET /api/users/me/profile (get my profile)
###      * PATCH /api/users/me/profile (update my profile)
###      * PATCH /api/users/me/mode (switch mode)
###    - Employee-only endpoints (requires employee JWT token):
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/verify/freelancer (verify as freelancer)
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/verify/client (verify as client)
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/unverify/freelancer (unverify as freelancer)
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/unverify/client (unverify as client)
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/suspend (suspend user)
###      * PATCH /api/users/:id/unsuspend (unsuspend user)

### 2. USER MODE
###    - Users can operate in two modes: "freelancer" or "client"
###    - Mode determines the user's primary role on the platform
###    - Users can switch between modes using the switch mode endpoint
###    - Default mode is "freelancer"

### 3. VERIFICATION STATUS
###    - isVerifiedAsFreelancer: User verified as a freelancer (employee action)
###    - isVerifiedAsClient: User verified as a client (employee action)
###    - Verification is independent for each role
###    - Users can be verified in both roles simultaneously

### 4. PROFILE UPDATE FIELDS
###    - name: String (1-100 characters, optional)
###    - overview: String (max 500 characters, optional, can be empty)
###    - jobTitle: String (max 100 characters, optional, can be empty)
###    - country: String (max 100 characters, optional, can be empty)
###    - address: String (max 500 characters, optional, can be empty)
###    - specificationId: UUID (optional, can be null)
###    - profilePicture: UUID (optional, can be null, references FileHub)
###    - skills: Array of UUIDs or comma-separated string (optional)
###    - tags: Array of UUIDs or comma-separated string (optional)
###    - available: Boolean (optional)
###    - At least one field must be provided

### 5. SKILLS AND TAGS
###    - Skills and tags are stored as arrays of UUIDs
###    - Can be provided as:
###      * Array: ["skill-uuid-1", "skill-uuid-2"]
###      * JSON string: "[\"skill-uuid-1\", \"skill-uuid-2\"]"
###      * Comma-separated string: "skill-uuid-1,skill-uuid-2"
###    - Skills reference the Skills table
###    - Tags reference the Tags table

### 6. PROFILE PICTURE
###    - profilePicture is a UUID that references FileHub
###    - File must be uploaded to S3 first using /api/s3/upload-url
###    - File purpose should be "profile"
###    - Use the fileId from the upload response

### 7. SEARCH AND FILTERING
###    - Search: Searches user names (case-insensitive, partial match)
###    - Filter by specification: Filter users by their specification
###    - Filter by mode: Filter by "freelancer" or "client"
###    - Filter by verification: Filter by verification status
###    - Multiple filters can be combined

### 8. SORTING
###    - sortBy: Field to sort by - "name", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "avgRating"
###    - sortOrder: "asc" or "desc"
###    - Default: sortBy="createdAt", sortOrder="desc"

### 9. PAGINATION
###    - page: Page number (default: 1, min: 1)
###    - limit: Items per page (default: 10, min: 1, max: 100)
###    - Response includes pagination metadata

### 10. SUSPENSION
###     - Suspended users have isSuspended set to true
###     - Suspension reason is required and stored
###     - Suspended users may have restricted access to platform features
###     - Only employees can suspend/unsuspend users

### 11. RELATED DATA
###     - getUserById and getMyProfile return related data:
###       * specification: Full specification object
###       * profilePictureData: FileHub object with URL and metadata (null if no picture)
###       * skillsData: Array of skill objects (fetched from skills UUIDs)
###       * tagsData: Array of tag objects (fetched from tags UUIDs)
###       * reviews: Array of review objects
###       * portfolio: Portfolio object
###       * previousWorkData: Array of previous work objects
###     - File data structure (profilePictureData):
###       {
###         "id": "file-uuid",
###         "url": "https://example.com/file.jpg",
###         "fileName": "file.jpg",
###         "fileType": "image",
###         "filePurpose": "profile",
###         "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
###         "fileSize": 102400,
###         "status": "ready",
###         "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###         "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###       }

### 12. ERROR RESPONSES
###     - 400 Bad Request: Invalid input data, validation errors
###     - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###     - 403 Forbidden: User doesn't have required role (employee)
###     - 404 Not Found: User not found
###     - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 13. USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Get All Freelancers
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?mode=freelancer&isVerifiedAsFreelancer=true&page=1&limit=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example 2: Search Users by Name
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?search=John&page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example 3: Get Users by Specification
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?specification=123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000&page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example 4: Update Profile with Skills
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/profile
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Updated Name",
  "skills": ["skill-uuid-1", "skill-uuid-2"],
  "available": true
}

### Example 5: Switch to Client Mode
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/mode
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "mode": "client"
}

### Example 6: Suspend a User
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000/suspend
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

{
  "suspendedReason": "Repeated violation of community guidelines"
}

### 14. DATA RELATIONSHIPS
###     - Users belong to a Specification (specificationId)
###     - Users have multiple Skills (skills array)
###     - Users have multiple Tags (tags array)
###     - Users can have a Portfolio (one-to-one)
###     - Users can have multiple Reviews (one-to-many)
###     - Users have a Profile Picture (profilePicture UUID references FileHub)

### 15. BEST PRACTICES
###     - Keep profile information up to date
###     - Use appropriate skills and tags for better discoverability
###     - Maintain a professional overview and job title
###     - Update availability status regularly
###     - Switch mode based on current needs (freelancer vs client)

### 16. INTEGRATION NOTES
###     - User data includes aggregated information (avgRating, totalReviews)
###     - Related data is fetched automatically for getUserById and getMyProfile
###     - Profile updates trigger updatedAt timestamp
###     - Suspended users may have restricted functionality
###     - Verification status affects user visibility and capabilities
